    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d988">

                <pb facs="0911" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg901"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163 Am 3/641: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsinan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hawthorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsinan</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-26T12:00:00+08:00">November 26,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 3—6:24 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my despatch No. 322 of March 11,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d988-f1"/>
                    third paragraph, Catholic Bishop of Tsinan was yesterday assured by senior
                    Japanese <pb facs="0912" n="902" xml:id="pg902"/> general here, upon approaching
                    the latter concerning the question, that American Catholic missionaries would
                    not be interned and would be permitted to continue their work in the event of
                    war between the United States and Japan.</p>
                <p>By mail to Peiping in code. Sent to the Department, repeated to Chungking. Code
                    text by air mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawthorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
